<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  BOV_Score__c Number -> Formula conversion, STEP 1 of 3 (SEVER + DELETE).
  POST-destructive companion of package.xml in this same directory -- see that
  file's header for the full wave rationale (why this is an in-place
  delete-and-recreate rather than the repo's usual additive rename pattern).

  STATUS: PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED FOR DEPLOY. The user deploys, not this repo.

  POST (not PRE): package.xml's 3 Apex edits stop reading/ordering by
  BOV_Score__c BEFORE this file's deletion runs in the same transaction, so by
  the time the field is dropped nothing left in the constructive payload still
  references it. This repo has measured that validating a destructive-only
  payload in isolation gives a FALSE "referenced elsewhere" failure (it diffs
  against live org state, which still has the old Apex) -- the ordering claim
  is only provable by a combined --manifest + --post-destructive-changes run,
  which is exactly what the dry-run below does.

  DELETES EXACTLY 1 CUSTOM FIELD:
    BOV_Submission__c.BOV_Score__c  (Number(4,0), nothing writes it, null on
    every row in the org)

  WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER (left for the org's automatic cleanup, matching
  this repo's e931e01 8-DateTime precedent): the field's own
  FieldPermissions rows on DPEG_Disposition_Edit / DPEG_Disposition_View are
  dropped by the platform when the field is deleted -- no destructive member
  needed for those, and no manifest entry exists for CustomFieldTranslation
  either (its local file is removed from the repo in this same commit, but
  translations are children of the field and are cleaned up automatically,
  same as e931e01).

  Deploy (only once authorised by the user; devops runs a validation-only
  dry-run first per standing project practice):
    sf project deploy start \
      --manifest manifest/bov-score-formula-conversion/package.xml \
      --post-destructive-changes manifest/bov-score-formula-conversion/destructiveChangesPost.xml \
      --target-org usman-dpeg \
      --test-level RunLocalTests --wait 30

  Do NOT pass --purge-on-delete -- documented elsewhere in this repo
  (manifest/portfolio-deal-a3) as non-functional on production orgs and
  failing silently rather than erroring. The field lands in the Recycle Bin,
  which is what Step 3's manual Erase step is for.

  Rollback: see package.xml's Rollback section in this same directory.
  -->
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <types>
        <members>BOV_Submission__c.BOV_Score__c</members>
        <name>CustomField</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
